  "report_period": "Week 9 (23rd Feb to 1st Mar 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Thenamaris have committed their Capesize \"Sealink\" 180/2010 Daehan, Korea (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) for USD 31 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-older \"Athenian Phoenix\" 179/2009 (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at region USD 23 mill. Moreover, the \"Star Audrey\" 175/2011 New Times, China (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) of Starbulk was committed to Greek interests at low-mid USD 27 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older \"Seamate\" 177/2010 SWS, China (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold in February at USD 26 mill. Following the sale of their Post Panamax \"Christine Oldendorff\" 93/2010 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) a month ago at USD 15,45 mill, clients of Oldendorff Carriers have now committed the sister vessel \"Conrad Oldendorff\" 93/2010 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Greek interests at USD 16,5 mill. Transocean Maritime Agencies have committed the Ultramax \"Andromeda\" 61/2011 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted) to Turkish interests at region USD 21 mill. For reference, the \"Shimanami Queen\" 61/2011 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in November at USD 18,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, clients of Abo Shoten have committed their \"ASL Fortune\" 58/2012 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 04/2027, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 19,3 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Solar Africa\" 58/2011 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 09/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold three weeks ago at USD 17,8 mill. Furthermore, the \"Konrad Schulte\" 55/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at low USD 16 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Melia 1\" 55/2011 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold in February at USD 17,8 mill. In addition, Densay Shipping committed their \"SSI Avenger\" 53/2004 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 10/2024, BWTS fitted) at USD 10,5 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Rui Fu Sheng\" 53/2003 Oshima, Japan (SS 11/2028, DD 11/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 8,5 mill. Chinese owners committed the OHBS Handysize \"Lucky Glory\" 32/2007 Kanda, Japan (SS 12/2027, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted) to Turkish interests at USD 10,3 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Lago Di Lugano\" 32/2008 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 10/2025) was sold recently at USD 10,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "No sales to report this week.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 11,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 17,000/20,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 16,000/18,000 pd range. A number of Indonesia and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 15,000/17.000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 17,000/20,000 pd. Continental trips into China were reported at the level of usd 25,000/27,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K/800K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesia trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 28,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 280K. Continental trips into Mediterranean with scrap were reported at the level of usd 19,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Continent-West Africa were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. US Gulf trips via South Africa into Japan were reported at the level of usd 26,000/28,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Baltic with iron ore were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. On the period front, a Supramax was reported fixed in the usd 15,400 pd 7/9 months employment basis delivery China with redelivery PG/Japan range.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000 pd. Trips from Black Sea into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
